Ladybird looks up a named zone’s offset at the local millisecond and
subtracts it from the unrounded epoch nanoseconds. SpiderMonkey’s
GetNamedTimeZoneEpochNanoseconds() calls MakeDate() for that
lookup and applies the result to GetUTCEpochNanoseconds(). V8’s
Intl::GetTimeZonePossibleOffsetNanoseconds() obtains ICU
offsets through ApproximateMillisecondEpoch(). JavaScriptCore’s
TemporalZonedDateTime::getEpochNanosecondsFor() delegates the
conversion to TemporalCore.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36 and Firefox 151.0 retained all nine fractional
digits in New York in 1600 and 2500 and in UTC just before 1970. The
WebKit 26.5 browser used for comparison didn’t expose Temporal.
